" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 27 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b4984b8-1073-51f4-bbe6-0c45bb082a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500491} {:answer/id #uuid "1601e7df-ddae-5494-a41c-da35e76fa3c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500516} {:answer/id #uuid "83748e6b-9023-5628-b878-282bfb4de93b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500739} {:answer/id #uuid "97e4106e-ea27-5370-8a2c-fa0b2b2c526d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500777} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7cb8ed-bc84-5b04-a0d8-47c0b7dd5e6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500491} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8b066b-e90d-5c38-b2a6-4d8b3185f0d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501048}] :question/id #uuid "ba29e43e-8fe2-5bbe-a64e-366d83a4fca9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97578" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d13c75-e6bc-5e2e-a8a5-6dd560e659ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549354} {:answer/id #uuid "209da59d-2b86-550d-89c6-5385f915b5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549381} {:answer/id #uuid "570944f0-ed2d-54ac-afa7-c23ef2d1f070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549492} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe4a7d2-be73-53f9-b806-31ea43cf2ba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549678} {:answer/id #uuid "d70dba8c-62c5-5199-93bd-0c9dd94ff141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549381} :answer-field/id #uuid "daee834d-972a-5370-8934-102b16e2168b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549906}] :question/id #uuid "15721919-affc-527a-806f-d54311da77ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-97580" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124543 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124352 :question/id #uuid "8a371b65-8c57-5d10-88aa-2d4928fb028c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5522" :question/problem "![](images/06/0609d1fd076c5913c8e26bf1dca823c60fb029ec5832ce34734dd4f80b82527d.svg)\n\nConsider the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ (shown above) and a basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\nThe matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^3$ relative to these bases, and the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2,$ are also given. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}},$ the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}.$ So, let\n\n![](images/a2/a244da85e128687b438d43ee49c8ee5b0bf864c0b36add61c382a7dff70dad66.svg)\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -18\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/ef/ef57f78641f939448e504b4ada6d538fef7a2800f130badb5c4970e3d2b1d4d1.svg)\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125130 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097573c5-6f6e-5470-bc18-c2bab540d7c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123381} {:answer/id #uuid "0c6183bd-41ba-5fa1-8e94-2e8531f0c384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123382} {:answer/id #uuid "102c9688-503b-5316-9709-91489515c42f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123383} {:answer/id #uuid "259581ee-9be3-5d0d-9877-d8815f3ab040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123384} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2f20e8-a6cd-59b3-8cbc-6b958b0a84ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123385}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ff8ce843-336b-5971-9e81-a5e48f7407f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123380}] :question/id #uuid "f7a57d38-b673-552d-85ae-a4e4b115b5bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-38535" :question/problem "$B = {\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}, [T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of $R^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of $R^{3}$.\nThe matrix $[T]_{B \\mid C}$ of the linear map $T: R^{2} → R^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x ∈ R^{2}$, are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125253 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d703106-8425-59f4-ab98-bbb498cc1ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360889} {:answer/id #uuid "a480ab57-0403-516c-ad58-20a01ffa8ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361571} {:answer/id #uuid "c08dee67-b612-5d80-aa49-ce955eee3566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-19 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361699} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ad8804-923c-52f4-b3f0-a74edc737064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361738} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0dffe9-0042-5ecf-9544-f545172f9c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360889} :answer-field/id #uuid "68281da4-1f1e-5fa7-ac18-8444248bc991" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362070}] :question/id #uuid "e241e927-1969-5b14-8d05-12ee0adb39d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-97587" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f3622ad-2ea7-574a-aba7-bff64babf1a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269530} {:answer/id #uuid "43bbbbe9-87fc-50fa-9ca4-b69afa75a220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269879} {:answer/id #uuid "5b93054f-5f47-5224-85f7-c46ce6379220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270083} {:answer/id #uuid "8b092faf-0a95-559c-b8a5-48878444af17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270473} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd8b2c9-59cf-55e7-b944-556a08fbae80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 76 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269879} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b57b72a-6d70-5a47-acab-9a518faa3f1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271673}] :question/id #uuid "b4e6c792-0bf4-5c85-ad37-7fcab89a66aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-140446" :question/problem "$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}},\\,[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} &=-15 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2} &=30.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 & -15 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 15\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336fb41f-4416-5b90-9963-63b715d894cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361063} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7b5d9e-e2af-5819-9157-eb95f22a5fe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361315} {:answer/id #uuid "860742e3-e187-5777-a59d-99f7335da169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361436} {:answer/id #uuid "d4184a13-5037-5335-bef6-cc89b6e2f44f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361788} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c815cc-4d5f-5de4-92b1-bdce9f7a0197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361873} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e0a7bfb-89f3-51f0-b3f7-efaec681dd46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362037}] :question/id #uuid "29ca0842-b657-584e-9ec2-fc1fbb7af353" :question/math-academy-id "q-97584" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\