ectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & -9 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0673faba-86e8-5a64-bfe1-0d525d80b6b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480123} {:answer/id #uuid "273d5980-25a9-5fc1-9c81-6904a3922563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480173} {:answer/id #uuid "598dc994-ad61-5fb4-b2d0-3ca9c1a22995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480261} {:answer/id #uuid "7e117b80-c1ef-555c-8c26-17c0cb6b419d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480318} {:answer/id #uuid "fddb317b-bc18-5964-bf6a-d4564de232a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480123} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4e63ab-bc23-5b80-b413-b0b8c109b3e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480627}] :question/id #uuid "a7b00f3c-cf97-5a00-9aea-1a5f4575fc82" :question/math-academy-id "q-38864" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=2{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1},\\,$ $T({b}_{2})=4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{3})=7{c}_{2}-5{c}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=2{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({b}_{2})=4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({b}_{3})=7{c}_{2}-5{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2})$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480694 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df95b1c-878e-5f9b-aa95-23cc414b629a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480137} {:answer/id #uuid "4282e852-2000-59cb-b403-01e0c9f8090a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -4 & 5 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480221} {:answer/id #uuid "466a2951-5ba8-50b4-a8bf-ec1d529c9752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480226} {:answer/id #uuid "572f320f-1169-58ad-b077-40d64f2de40a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480259} {:answer/id #uuid "80c66b22-25ce-5572-a11f-1d4c843a628e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 5 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480259} :answer-field/id #uuid "10e1ecc1-0f34-5e80-bdc2-1d29879f9be1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480539}] :question/id #uuid "d65cfc4f-129a-584c-86e4-865a0ea5e2d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-140426" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=6{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=-5{c}_{2}+9{c}_{3}-4{c}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=6{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({b}_{2})=-5{c}_{2}+9{c}_{3}-4{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and  $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501158 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "394529b7-5240-5ff7-90db-e1add45b32a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500582} {:answer/id #uuid "825811a4-08b5-5ffb-990f-7e501d2498b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500736} {:answer/id #uuid "9efa7096-ec71-5ba8-a546-d69b56f674bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500789} {:answer/id #uuid "aad3aeef-b512-5754-9b36-a0105a67e7d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500820} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f6fe27-6dff-5e8f-81fc-28e28ad0e3ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500736} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b795f03-1c4c-51ce-9ec3-51380c3631d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501074}] :question/id #uuid "3a497a8c-181f-5ddb-8e0c-d7f0dcc66829" :question/math-academy-id "q-38861" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2},\\,$ $T({b}_{2})={c}_{1}-4{c}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{3})=5{c}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({b}_{2})={c}_{1}-4{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({b}_{3})=5{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2})$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124604 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124416 :question/id #uuid "3d6b0aec-c282-581e-ae4a-560654d80e3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8605" :question/problem "Consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3\\}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ given by\n![](images/32/324c42ad6277fdf7b59b1ec9ceed977debe4d659187624a261a0e7175911c1dd.svg)\n\nFind the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ relative to these bases if \n![](images/90/903982d37fc42c27b8ded5d6de1189c2407a1ee2183019d25fe86b47813e38b5.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2),$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_i)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n![](images/79/79119f75c40495aebb7b37013c8a390dbf52eaeec501e62a965d3e5925d51f35.svg)\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 11 & -29 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/2a/2aa5592cc6346c444c0a49b8e3a6266c509adc13b2b8be10fdf0b43af6fbd220.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125131 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1209e78-1f07-505d-a10d-09c065bc8bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123387} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b4dfd1-8922-590b-9f00-a74e289139ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123388} {:answer/id #uuid "da49a8f0-0c4e-56d7-905d-2d89c5e87623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123389} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb38b5d-c48d-5726-a40c-f40a08cc9f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123390} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7a6f62-cbef-50f4-afa3-083d158bb1ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123391}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9793e473-a841-5f78-ac9b-1aaa5e051fed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eecc0631-492f-564e-ad61-4de8bd9f9cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366073} {:answer/id #uuid "1311c295-fcc4-5f43-addd-d8ba93860600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366074} {:answer/id #uuid "a0276032-b012-50d6-824f-9ff9bef2d6a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366075} {:answer/id #uuid "5a95deca-9cea-53df-a322-15594c3aac83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366076} {:answer/id #uuid "84373611-2f1b-5228-9984-5dae52ce34ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366076} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfbc19cc-2a3f-5d05-a587-d4ee526efced" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366072}] :question/id #uuid "08c908af-7130-5cf2-98cf-692a2e7de637" :question/math-academy-id "q-38567" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,T({b}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,T({b}_{3})=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 3 & 21\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125142 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815bb8b4-b2cd-58f7-ae1a-41b9a8d8e20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123453} {:answer/id #uuid "e29bae0f-ca74-51ee-b510-20b94bee6e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123454} {:answer/id #uuid "ec1fcffe-8bfe-5322-8ca5-65caeb723b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\