C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -11 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a507e0d-3567-5d61-bbe2-9d89591f6ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364991} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6167bb-8811-5823-8e3c-9c0a0fd96728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364992} {:answer/id #uuid "535b4647-2e3c-57e3-87ae-e2d55ffa67b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 & 12 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364993} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8e09ea-3cbb-5e01-b44d-76870dd03f37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364994} {:answer/id #uuid "a4772a99-ebf0-5414-abdd-91369dd717ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 & 12 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :