n{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}7-3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e41392-8432-5b22-aa41-0cdff945ff9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395625} {:answer/id #uuid "39141340-98a9-5f1f-9ceb-ac060eb31c83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395626} {:answer/id #uuid "ae413a9c-9e4a-59ae-929e-836cd2bae3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395627} {:answer/id #uuid "4e2c5c24-6fc9-5369-b94a-28c4783d6010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395628} {:answer/id #uuid "b902a495-b6c7-53b3-b3fd-d5da866abbdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395628} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef87be86-0ce8-57a7-8fde-951ee2f08f12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395624}] :question/id #uuid "7cb64545-86e3-59aa-b0fe-7ccf30353d96" :question/math-academy-id "q-99339" :question/problem "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1+3\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096e7527-4c01-5dce-8ff8-e0db3c75370d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410832} {:answer/id #uuid "0a8fe61d-12cc-5e71-bf5f-8ade179fac6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410834} {:answer/id #uuid "1c87451a-2d1c-5373-8af0-e4594174b876" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410836} {:answer/id #uuid "5113c383-2506-5331-9225-ebb1f5af24a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410840} {:answer/id #uuid "f16edcb8-7daa-5bb4-b079-ab44c7accef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410850} :answer-field/id #uuid "8400b796-2f04-536c-986d-13f15ae5b122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410852}] :question/id #uuid "d6880ebc-9daa-5cd0-b5d7-2100fa039d06" :question/math-academy-id "q-99345" :question/problem "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4+3\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12fab1be-92c3-5c73-9057-2ce01cfa87cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561641} {:answer/id #uuid "1b236a4d-fc2f-53b6-af86-4c4f9793792b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561656} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca133f2-63fd-5e30-bf07-bb0ae8d8988a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561777} {:answer/id #uuid "66b397cb-7b81-5983-a6b0-49e027e16f2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561836} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5d726b-4c91-5de1-b99c-cbf38e533e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561641} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fea878e-a991-5b88-82fa-0dff5d838738" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562229}] :question/id #uuid "fed17ade-b98f-5b7e-aa56-3747d2eae8ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-99343" :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-4+3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3-2\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Matrix to Rotation-Scaling Form Given Multiple Parts of the Decomposition"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129135 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128946 :question/id #uuid "26e641c9-bda5-5b93-8137-f4ec744ddb5c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5531" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f341a3893509e9adc2b5897e14a87656aa3c49824dda809ae6030646c6ece79.svg)\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PCP^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2 \\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PCP^{-1},$ where \n\n![](images/48/489a26b52ac132d82ffa918d931963a0cd33df092aea8e70885dc41c4e363be5.svg)\n\nand $\\mathbf{v}$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda.$\n\n- From the matrix ![](images/bf/bfc2be5324b72df4c3c63e92c4501bbda6b0fcde0ef8e6284d739db51e73a722.svg) we deduce that $\\textrm{Re}(\\lambda)={\\color{blue}3}$ and $\\textrm{Im}(\\lambda) = {\\color{red}-1}.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda = {\\color{blue}3}+({\\color{red}-1})\\text{i} = 3-\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix ![](images/1f/1fd5d191e88cd5f00ffd91f83800ce0c82024cedea60bf78432cd0abb504252a.svg) we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n![](images/df/df9978ae9ef1bb16b79e36abace84ef559ef64b6aa9e47369ae7efc5ecf7da27.svg)\n\nFinally, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda,$ and the second eigenvector must be the complex conjugate of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nTherefore, our eigenvalues and eigenvectors are \n\n![](images/81/811faf0baa4ae081f2f5ae9064a060f979ae553df5e5e156028e91b3038a4a2b.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1dcdd3f4-c03e-5887-a493-05598dbe4fc3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a4cb808-0d2a-5594-9b85-ff404df60569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 1 ± 4\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}± 4\\textrm{i} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127460} {:answer/id #uuid "c0435814-fcd3-519e-9a31-416a2e84845b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = ± \\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}± \\textrm{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127461} {:answer/id #uuid "efa7c538-1fef-55d8-b047-5314f9573a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-4∓\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}± \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127462} {:answer/id #uuid "2467ebf5-0c70-544f-ab7e-03adea208cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 1 ± 4\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}± 4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127463} {:answer/id #uuid "451febc3-3227-5bfa-9861-8f41f7e4ecc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-4∓\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ ± \\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127464}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e44acb2e-3642-5a90-bbfc-354d89d65821" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127459}] :question/id #uuid "a5ce82cf-ed2b-58ed-86e3-cd65804baa05" :question/math-academy-id "q-38559" :question/problem "$P = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A = PCP^{-1}$, what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a44df2bc-f14f-59a2-a672-6f0e6bb9920f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 5∓2\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 ± 4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127754} {:answer/id #uuid "df507133-b25f-5b28-ba47-8c4a2f3d63c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 2 ± 5\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 ± 4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127755} {:answer/id #uuid "12c35eb9-f22b-5303-ba37-a36c95e38a27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-1∓4\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}2 ± 5\\textrm{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127756} {:answer/id #uuid "137bdf37-6094-5b37-bef7-d0150c3ee24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 5∓2\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}4 ± \\textrm{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127757} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea63856-d4a2-5c1e-848c-4ccd15dd67b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-1 ± 4\\textrm{i}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}5 ± 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127758}] :answer-field/id #uuid "691b3425-43de-571e-82e4-0da7a888fe7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127753} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df8d6616-7589-5370-bc49-52a7bb7f8cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-1\\pm 4\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}5\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402670} {:answer/id #uuid "a4bb7193-9b8a-57fb-b9c2-0684422071d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5∓2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402671} {:answer/id #uuid "e2edf1c3-9b45-5eb1-956f-0e32c947cd8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-1∓4\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\pm 5\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402672} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e8e799-40bd-5e8d-bdf8-8f7da833a824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5∓2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402673} {:answer/id #uuid "afe8e21b-415e-59ff-afb5-394f16c6b1c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2\\pm 5\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5∓2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402673} :answer-field/id #uuid "513ddfff-da03-5d7b-9d28-423b0f581b95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402669}] :question/id #uuid "a0d796fd-8159-54fb-b817-7bb654ebaf53" :question/math-academy-id "q-39130" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\n- From the matrix $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -(-2) & 5\\end{bmatrix},$ we deduce that $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=5$ and $\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=-2.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda =5+(-2)\\text{i}=5-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix $P=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},$ we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 3+0\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda ,$ and the second eigenvector must be the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nTherefore, our eigenvalues and eigenvectors are \n\n$$\n\\lambda =5∓2\\text{i},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae5ed35-dd79-5b41-8722-6cf9fa2af9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2∓7\\text{i}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1∓2\\text{i} \\\\ -3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324066} {:answer/id #uuid "40253d1c-0a5f-5a16-8ff3-1c8ede9187fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2∓7\\text{i}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1∓2\\text{i} \\\\ -3∓2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324485} {:answer/id #uuid "60582d8b-a31f-5d7f-bb71-14179b0593a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7\\pm 2\\text{i}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\pm \\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324775} {:answer/id #uuid "7cef3f3c-8d15-5b9d-ba9c-b2d90d708175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7∓2\\text{i}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2∓\\text{i} \\\\ -3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325025} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce2021a-5442-56b1-8c61-8979e8fe78f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7∓2\\text{i}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1∓2\\text{i} \\\\ -3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7∓2\\text{i}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1∓2\\text{i} \\\\ -3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325167} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0266539-ca32-5360-9e7c-f029b99c6adb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326565}] :question/id #uuid "aeba3951-f78a-5761-99ba-31